- start/target labelled by OSM street names at the node (ID kept in tooltip);
- closed segments listed with name, length, access and per-segment 'show'/'remove';
- each interval shows period, duration and state at analysis time; date inputs folded;
- A/B overview: what is closed, when, active or not;
- camera: every automatic move saves the user's view; 'return' restores it; after
  compare the map stays put unless the route is entirely off-screen;
- schedule table: A and B for every interval segment via existing POST /compare;
- technical digests/IDs moved into <details>.

